---
title: Cornflour Sponge Cake
servings: 8
time: 35 min
tags: baking, cake, sponge, dessert, australian
cuisine: Australian
course: dessert
source: received_1510215013882701.JPG
---

Preheat oven to 375°F (190°C). Grease and flour a #large springform pan{}.

In a #clean bowl{}, beat @egg whites{4} until stiff and foamy.

Gradually add @sugar{3/4%cup} while continuing to beat until very thick and glossy.

Add @egg yolks{4} and beat well until thoroughly combined.

Sift in @cornflour{1%cup}(or custard powder), additional @cornflour{2%tbsp}, @baking soda{1/2%tsp}, and @cream of tartar{1%tsp}. Gently fold into the egg mixture until just combined.

Pour batter into the prepared pan.

Bake at 375°F for ~cake{20%minutes}. The cake should just leave the sides of the tin when cooked.

Immediately upon removing from the oven, drop the cake pan flat from knee height onto the floor or counter to release trapped steam and keep the light sponge structure from collapsing.
